Track 1: Stained Panes Gulp the Meltwater
- Story & Context: During an impromptu solstice gig inside the Briksdalsbreen cave system, accordionist Torbjørn Vik rigged his amplifier directly against an unstable wall of turquoise ice just as the ceiling began weeping thick sheets of condensation. The sensory shock of sub-zero runoff trickling down the necks of eighty packed revelers catalyzed a frenzied, foot-stomping pit rather than a panic. As the down-tuned guitars crashed into an ecstatic 175-BPM polka, Torbjørn roared over the roar of falling ice chunks, "Drink the blue sky before the rafters give away!" That drenched, chaotic triumph proved that subterranean meltwater could become the rhythmic heart of a triumphant new dance.
