Track 2: Thermal Shock in D-Minor
- Story & Context: In the makeshift glassblower's shed at Nigardsbreen, lead singer Solveig Bratt attempted to fuse colored glass rondels inside an annealing kiln while singing along to the band's rehearsals over a blaring monitor wedge. When a blast of freezing meltwater surged beneath the door and struck the kiln's iron floor, the sudden thermal clash shattered every vessel with high-pitched, singing fractures that matched the pitch of her vocal warmups. Instead of mourning the lost work, she laughed, climbed atop an overturned wooden crate, and belt-confessed into the cavern acoustics, "A shattered pane lets twice the morning in!" The recorded track immortalized her soaring, brass-backed coloratura woven seamlessly with the brittle, percussive pop of cooling slag.
